        "reason": "Type B cast defect: TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP(REGEXP_REPLACE(col, offset-strip), \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss[.SSSSSS]\") returns NULL on any shape the pinned format misses (date-only values especially), and TRY_ makes it silent -- those NULLs reach the judge as differing_null_only/gap_shaped, i.e. a parse failure disguised as a FHIR coverage gap at the lower bar. Replace every datetime mapping with a bare TRY_CAST(col AS TIMESTAMP_NTZ). See pathling-sql SKILL.md and MIMIC_NOTES.md:337.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_justification": "Judge-accepted intrinsic contested divergence: MedicationAdministration.identifier is not populated by mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_medication_administration_icu.sql:42-100, so inputevents.linkorderid has no FHIR element or recoverable representation and the declared typed NULL explains the 8,510 null-only rows. The same ETL casts naive inputevents starttime/endtime through TIMESTAMPTZ at lines 8-9 and writes those normalized values at lines 64-65, irreversibly shifting DST-gap 02:28 values to 03:28; UUID construction at line 20 excludes timestamps, so the two key shifts and one endtime conflict cannot be recovered by any FHIR query. Representable fidelity is 8,510/8,513 (99.9648%), excluding linkorderid.",
        "superseded_status": "COMPLETED_WITH_DIVERGENCE"
